ComfyUI-Hy-Nomas

This package ports Tencent's Hy-Nomas inference code (https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hy-Nomas, commit 18974d4,
Apache License 2.0; see docs/upstream/LICENSE-HY-NOMAS) to ComfyUI.

Copied or closely ported from it (Apache-2.0, modified for ComfyUI):
- hy_nomas/prompt.py: prompt shaping from hymm/inference.py and the action-offset logic of hymm/pipeline/base.py
- hy_nomas/model.py: the DiT of hymm/models/dit/nomas_cpt.py and its modules (rewritten for ComfyUI ops)
- hy_nomas/world.py: history frame selection from hymm/models/dit/modules/uniform_history_cache.py and the INT8
  KV format of int8_kv_cache.py
- hy_nomas/camera.py: pose normalization and resampling from hymm/models/camera/geometry/demo_precomputed.py,
  rotation_scale.py and discretize_poses.py; the key controls follow apps/frontend CameraPathDrawer.tsx
- hy_nomas/pixelumm.py: the PixelUMM decoder of hymm/models/vae/pixelumm_decoder/ (itself a port of
  nv-tlabs/PixelUMM, Apache-2.0 code)
- hy_nomas/dcae.py: the DCAE-V encoder of hymm/models/vae/autoencoder_dcae_v.py
- docs/upstream/*.yaml and example_prompts.json: Tencent's configuration and example prompt

Model weights are not included. Hy-Nomas weights are released by Tencent under the Apache License 2.0. The PixelUMM
decoder weights (and fine-tunes of them) are under the NVIDIA One-Way Noncommercial License: non-commercial research
and evaluation use only.

T8 derivative integration, By T8star, 2026-10-26.
Based on PedroMarinhoDev/ComfyUI-Hy-Nomas, commit 712614ecf1d57a7159f9ab96b7894152f3195a26.
Modifications: explicit CPU KV archive budgets and statistics, native ComfyUI budget/cache nodes,
sampling/history and PixelUMM layout cleanup on cancellation or failure, transactional Drive state updates,
bounded CPU text cache, budgeted workflow examples, and CPU lifecycle regression tests.
The original code remains under GPL-3.0 and the upstream notices and license files are retained.
This derivative does not use the upstream author's Comfy Registry PublisherId.
2026-10-26 T8 path compatibility: configure Triton cache path knobs through Python
for Windows Unicode environment paths; see hy_nomas/platform_compat.py.
T8 additionally reserves resolution/window-based decoder activation memory through ComfyUI model management, blends streaming output on the CPU, and exposes decode-window progress; model weights and arithmetic modes are unchanged.
T8 unloads idle model residency before native sampling, exposes World tensors to ComfyUI's RAM cache accounting, and preserves renamed files in model selectors. The bundled launchers disable pinned memory and asynchronous offload; user-specified model folders take precedence over bundled folders with the same filenames.
T8 bounds INT8 KV quantization temporaries in token chunks and uses a single FP32 CPU output buffer for full IMAGE decoding, preserving the original per-token scales, rounding and BF16 overlap blending. Decoder loading explicitly unloads idle models first.
The Windows bundled bootstrap sets default mimalloc purge/arena-commit environment options before PyTorch initialization; standalone node installation requires the host startup environment to set these options.
Full IMAGE decoding requests CPU output/workspace headroom through ComfyUI's RAM pressure cache callback. Current inputs retain their normal executor ownership; evicted upstream results may be recomputed on later use.
